PRE-EXISTING BASELINE BREAKAGE FIXED (covenant #8 — could not build on red):
  ShellWindow.xaml.cs had two malformed PageFactory.Register lambdas committed on this branch —
  the YearReview and AutomationList blocks were missing their `return page; });` closures, which
  caused an 84-error XAML-compiler cascade (every Components/UI type reported "Unknown type" because
  the assembly's C# failed to compile). The two closures were restored to their correct form (the
  lambda bodies + referenced symbols GoBack/ParseYearParam/NavigateTo/CloseRequested/NavigationRequested
  all already existed). Verified: full-solution build went 84 errors → 0. This file is the
  NavigationView-registration target this unit must edit anyway, so the fix is in-scope.

NOTE on idealized paths: the prompt header lists an idealized output path
(apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Charging/*.xaml). The real repo is a C#-markup WinUI 3 app —
every sibling W7 page (BatteryDegradation, VehicleCost, TrueCost, Timeline, WeeklyDigest, ApiLogs,
FeedbackQueue, SchemaDrift, EnergyFlow, YearReview) lives under
apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Page>/ as <Page>.{Model,Source,ViewModel}.cs + <Page>.cs
(no per-page .xaml). This unit follows that established convention exactly (verified against
BatteryDegradationPage). Pure logic lives in the WinUI-free .Model/.Source/.ViewModel (unit-tested
headlessly via the .csproj <Compile Include> seam); the .cs is the thin view, exercised by the app build.

